WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.760
good morning John

00:00:00.840 --> 00:00:01.800
I'm still sick

00:00:02.280 --> 00:00:03.400
this is annoying

00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:06.700
the thing that I've noticed now that I've had this happening for like two weeks

00:00:06.700 --> 00:00:07.220
is that when you are sick

00:00:07.220 --> 00:00:08.400
people give you advice

00:00:08.400 --> 00:00:10.620
I've actually noticed this for years when it comes to my ulcerative colitis

00:00:10.780 --> 00:00:12.800
a lot of people seem to have a cure

00:00:12.920 --> 00:00:14.160
in their back pocket

00:00:14.220 --> 00:00:16.540
if only I'd go gluten free or stop eating grains

00:00:16.620 --> 00:00:18.340
or palio or vegan

00:00:18.340 --> 00:00:20.660
or stop eating short train carbohydrates

00:00:20.780 --> 00:00:24.040
or fast for three days and then eat an apple

00:00:24.080 --> 00:00:26.080
seriously it was a whole thing

00:00:26.080 --> 00:00:28.360
and it took like half the party for him to explain it to me

00:00:28.360 --> 00:00:30.480
and over the years I've tried a lot of those things

00:00:30.480 --> 00:00:32.000
and none of them worked

00:00:32.000 --> 00:00:34.280
what worked was taking the medicine that my doctor gave to me

00:00:34.280 --> 00:00:34.820
and then over the past week

00:00:34.820 --> 00:00:36.960
people have been saying completely normal things to me

00:00:36.960 --> 00:00:38.960
like get some rest man

00:00:38.960 --> 00:00:40.680
or take it easy

00:00:40.680 --> 00:00:42.440
stop stressing sleep more

00:00:42.440 --> 00:00:45.060
and I've been a little bit shocked by how annoying this is

00:00:45.060 --> 00:00:46.960
not because it is annoying like its fine

00:00:46.960 --> 00:00:48.600
It's a totally fine thing for somebody to say

00:00:48.600 --> 00:00:51.480
but it's tapping into this thing that I have

00:00:51.480 --> 00:00:53.220
with my ulcerative colitis

00:00:53.220 --> 00:00:54.960
after years of dealing with my chronic illness

00:00:55.080 --> 00:00:55.580
that I can not cure

00:00:55.580 --> 00:00:57.700
and having people tell me ways that I should be able to cure it

00:00:57.700 --> 00:01:02.160
what I'm hearing is not, you know 'take it easy, we support you'

00:01:02.280 --> 00:01:06.760
instead I'm hearing: 'I have the secret to your wellness and If only

00:01:06.920 --> 00:01:10.620
'you had the courage and fortitude to implement it, you would no longer be sick'

00:01:10.620 --> 00:01:12.220
and one step further from that

00:01:12.220 --> 00:01:13.520
whats tickling by subconscious here

00:01:13.620 --> 00:01:17.160
is this idea that my illness is my fault

00:01:17.340 --> 00:01:19.540
I know that my chronic illness is pretty insignificant

00:01:19.540 --> 00:01:21.060
compared with what a lot of other people are dealing with

00:01:21.060 --> 00:01:23.520
but I think this is probably an experience that a lot of people have

00:01:23.520 --> 00:01:27.160
when you tell me, a person who has lived with ulcerative colitis for more than a decade

00:01:27.160 --> 00:01:29.480
that you have the secret to my wellness

00:01:29.480 --> 00:01:31.400
I can not help but dislike you

00:01:31.400 --> 00:01:33.480
like if that's my first impression, and sometimes it is

00:01:33.580 --> 00:01:35.320
I'm like 'I'm out'

00:01:35.420 --> 00:01:40.100
and look maybe this is the one weird instance in which you are the one who was right

00:01:40.100 --> 00:01:42.720
and maybe I'm missing that opportunity

00:01:42.720 --> 00:01:44.020
to finally make myself better

00:01:44.020 --> 00:01:45.480
but I've heard this line so many times

00:01:45.480 --> 00:01:49.320
with so many different facts and so many different pieces of anecdotal evidence

00:01:49.480 --> 00:01:52.360
that all I can hear when people say this to me

00:01:52.540 --> 00:01:54.620
is 'your illness is your fault'

00:01:54.620 --> 00:01:56.680
because we want it to be somethings fault, right?

00:01:56.680 --> 00:02:01.940
because if its not the fault of anything, then it has to be just weird random chance

00:02:01.940 --> 00:02:03.520
and that's what chronic illness is

00:02:03.520 --> 00:02:04.920
it just freaking happens

00:02:04.920 --> 00:02:08.980
to good people and bad people and champion athletes and people who drink to much

00:02:08.980 --> 00:02:12.160
I've dealt with my illness by allowing myself to accept it

00:02:12.160 --> 00:02:17.640
by admitting to myself and accepting that my life is different now and my body is different now

00:02:17.640 --> 00:02:19.580
and I have to live inside of this body

00:02:19.580 --> 00:02:20.780
that sometimes hurts itself

00:02:20.780 --> 00:02:22.500
science will keep marching forward

00:02:22.500 --> 00:02:27.180
and someday maybe there will be a medicine that I can take that will control this disease

00:02:27.180 --> 00:02:29.020
without making me sick in other ways

00:02:29.020 --> 00:02:33.860
and yes, science shows that my behaviour does influence the expression of my disease

00:02:33.860 --> 00:02:36.000
and so does my experience of my disease

00:02:36.180 --> 00:02:39.240
and so I do need support from people that help me make the decisions

00:02:39.360 --> 00:02:41.380
that my doctor says that I should make

00:02:41.540 --> 00:02:43.620
and that I have decided for myself that I want to make

00:02:43.740 --> 00:02:47.080
but I also can't avoid the truth that this is the body that I'm in

00:02:47.180 --> 00:02:49.480
and I have to accept that like among the

00:02:49.480 --> 00:02:53.500
many probabilities that were cast, that mostly came up in my favour

00:02:53.500 --> 00:02:55.500
I rolled bad on auto-immune diseases

00:02:55.520 --> 00:02:59.480
my brain tried to tell me over and over again that this is my fault

00:02:59.700 --> 00:03:02.260
I have searched for every possible way

00:03:02.340 --> 00:03:03.640
subconsciously and consciously

00:03:03.740 --> 00:03:05.500
that this is a thing that I did to myself

00:03:05.620 --> 00:03:07.460
and that's a crappy feeling

00:03:07.460 --> 00:03:10.660
and its re-emphasized every time someone tells me that there's a

00:03:10.660 --> 00:03:13.100
simple thing that I can do to make myself well

00:03:13.180 --> 00:03:14.180
I want to say here at the end of this video

00:03:14.280 --> 00:03:17.160
I'm doing fine, I'm not angry or frustrated

00:03:17.240 --> 00:03:19.160
at my friends or at you

00:03:19.160 --> 00:03:21.640
I have a loving and supportive group of people

00:03:21.640 --> 00:03:22.880
who are fantastic in my life

00:03:22.880 --> 00:03:25.560
and I do my best to understand that when people are saying these things

00:03:25.560 --> 00:03:28.200
they're not trying to make me feel what I'm feeling

00:03:28.200 --> 00:03:30.960
so I just try and accept that support for what it is

00:03:30.960 --> 00:03:33.480
rather than how it's being expressed specifically

00:03:33.480 --> 00:03:36.220
but if you want to be supportive of someone who's sick in your life

00:03:36.220 --> 00:03:38.340
make sure that you recognise that it's very possible

00:03:38.340 --> 00:03:39.800
that they are struggling right now

00:03:39.800 --> 00:03:44.640
with this feeling that they did something to cause or to deserve the illness they have

00:03:44.720 --> 00:03:46.700
even if objectively they understand that that's completely untrue

00:03:46.700 --> 00:03:49.700
when we say there is an easy way out of this

00:03:49.700 --> 00:03:50.380
and there's not

00:03:50.380 --> 00:03:51.800
what we're making people feel

00:03:51.800 --> 00:03:53.480
is that 'this is your fault'

00:03:53.560 --> 00:03:54.680
when it's not.

00:03:54.680 --> 00:03:55.901
John, I'll see you on tuesday

